1
00:00:02,290 --> 00:00:04,040
[footsteps]

2
00:00:05,920 --> 00:00:07,840
[YURU (YOUNG)]
Father, what is this?

3
00:00:07,880 --> 00:00:10,930
A passageway that connects
the Left and Right to the keep.

4
00:00:10,970 --> 00:00:12,140
This was always here?

5
00:00:12,180 --> 00:00:13,760
[MINE] A long time ago,

6
00:00:13,810 --> 00:00:15,930
when this village
was still a castle,

7
00:00:15,970 --> 00:00:18,640
the lord had this
secret passageway made.

8
00:00:18,690 --> 00:00:21,150
Only a select few people
knew of it.

9
00:00:21,610 --> 00:00:23,820
Be sure not to tell
anyone else about it

10
00:00:23,860 --> 00:00:26,690
and avoid using it unless
you have no other choice.

11
00:00:29,110 --> 00:00:31,320
The Left and Right's bases
at the village exit

12
00:00:31,360 --> 00:00:33,070
are directly above us.

13
00:00:34,580 --> 00:00:35,620
[Yuru (young) gasps]

14
00:00:35,660 --> 00:00:37,580
Listen to me, Yuru.

15
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:40,210
Know that no matter
what happens in the future,

16
00:00:40,250 --> 00:00:43,420
the Left and Right
are watching over you.

17
00:00:43,460 --> 00:00:45,250
[Right chuckles]
We've been watchin' you

18
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:46,760
this whole time, Yuru.

19
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:49,630
Henceforth, we will be
lending our power to you,

20
00:00:49,670 --> 00:00:50,970
as your daemons.

21
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:53,550
The Left and the Right.

22
00:00:53,590 --> 00:00:54,800
Is that you?

23
00:00:56,470 --> 00:00:59,100
[♪ opening theme song playing]

24
00:01:08,780 --> 00:01:10,860
DAEMONS OF THE SHADOW REALM

25
00:02:26,310 --> 00:02:27,400
[Right grunts]

26
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:29,610
So, Left, can this
sniveling brat

27
00:02:29,650 --> 00:02:31,190
truly be our Master?

28
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:34,780
Enough of your prattling, Right.
Our master seems ill at ease.

29
00:02:34,820 --> 00:02:36,360
[DERA] My humblest greetings.

30
00:02:36,410 --> 00:02:38,200
Honored to meet you.

31
00:02:38,240 --> 00:02:39,910
You're Dera, the retainer.

32
00:02:39,950 --> 00:02:42,450
We've long had our eyes
on you as well.

33
00:02:42,660 --> 00:02:44,830
Now tell me.
We took down those birds

34
00:02:44,870 --> 00:02:47,920
because they seemed a threat
to our master,

35
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:49,340
but what were they?

36
00:02:49,380 --> 00:02:51,920
[DERA] They're vehicles
of the modern world below.

37
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:53,840
Look, we're short on time
right now.

38
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:56,680
There's some scary folks here,
at least two.

39
00:02:56,720 --> 00:02:59,300
Help us get down the mountain
quickly and safely,

40
00:02:59,350 --> 00:03:01,430
-and then I'll explain.
-[RIGHT] Watch it.

41
00:03:01,470 --> 00:03:04,100
Only our master
gets to order us around.

42
00:03:04,140 --> 00:03:06,520
And that title
does not belong to you.

43
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:09,810
-We heed Yuru alone.
-[DERA] Yeah, I know that!

44
00:03:09,860 --> 00:03:12,070
But I can't get him up to speed
right now!

45
00:03:12,110 --> 00:03:13,570
-[GABBY] Lame.
-[Yuru gasps]

46
00:03:14,150 --> 00:03:16,490
[GABBY] They look like
a pair of toughies.

47
00:03:16,530 --> 00:03:19,280
So whose daemons are you,
Old Dude's?

48
00:03:19,320 --> 00:03:20,950
[YURU] What is that
tooth monster?

49
00:03:20,990 --> 00:03:22,910
[DERA] Crap,
they're here already!

50
00:03:22,950 --> 00:03:25,540
How are you unscathed
after a friggin' grenade?

51
00:03:25,580 --> 00:03:27,750
Sorry, but these chompers
can take a hit.

52
00:03:27,790 --> 00:03:30,040
And they're not "monsters."
Rude.

53
00:03:30,090 --> 00:03:32,090
Let's see.

54
00:03:32,550 --> 00:03:35,470
You look to be about 16.
Are you this Yuru kid?

55
00:03:35,510 --> 00:03:37,680
I am, but I'm 17.

56
00:03:37,720 --> 00:03:40,720
No, not in their world.
Only by traditional counting.

57
00:03:40,760 --> 00:03:41,850
[YURU] How so?

58
00:03:42,010 --> 00:03:45,310
Well then. Asa's brother
is alive after all.

59
00:03:45,680 --> 00:03:46,770
Asa?

60
00:03:46,810 --> 00:03:48,350
[Yuru grunts]

61
00:03:51,060 --> 00:03:53,360
[ASA] I'm gonna kill
everybody else.

62
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:55,440
-[Gabriel growls]
-Make this easy

63
00:03:55,490 --> 00:03:56,610
and come with me.

64
00:03:56,650 --> 00:03:58,280
[Yuru grunts]

65
00:03:58,610 --> 00:04:01,370
The village massacre,
that was you?

66
00:04:01,410 --> 00:04:02,910
You caught me.

67
00:04:03,450 --> 00:04:06,080
Master Yuru,
just give us the order,

68
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:08,790
and you have our full strength
at your command.

69
00:04:08,830 --> 00:04:10,830
[YURU] Order you? No way.

70
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:11,880
[RIGHT] Huh?

71
00:04:12,170 --> 00:04:14,090
[YURU] You're the village's
sacred guardians.

72
00:04:14,130 --> 00:04:16,340
I wouldn't dare
overstep my place.

73
00:04:16,380 --> 00:04:18,260
[Gabby sighs]

74
00:04:18,300 --> 00:04:20,380
[YURU] I won't make demands,

75
00:04:20,430 --> 00:04:22,260
but I do have two requests.

76
00:04:22,680 --> 00:04:26,470
First, please look for
any survivors in the village.

77
00:04:26,520 --> 00:04:28,980
If you would, take them
somewhere safe.

78
00:04:29,770 --> 00:04:32,610
Second, more personally,

79
00:04:33,270 --> 00:04:35,940
I want to kill the runt myself.
Don't touch her.

80
00:04:35,980 --> 00:04:37,530
[Gabby grunts]

81
00:04:37,570 --> 00:04:41,820
Aside from that, it's up to you.
Do as you both please.

82
00:04:41,870 --> 00:04:43,280
[Right laughs]

83
00:04:43,320 --> 00:04:45,120
Do you hear that? Lucky us!

84
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:48,370
Seems like our new boss
is the hands-off type!

85
00:04:48,910 --> 00:04:50,120
I can work with that!

86
00:04:50,170 --> 00:04:51,210
EPISODE 2
"LEFT AND RIGHT"

87
00:04:53,920 --> 00:04:55,840
[clattering]

88
00:04:57,420 --> 00:04:59,300
[Yamaha grunting]

89
00:05:01,090 --> 00:05:02,890
-[ASA] Old witch.
-[YAMAHA] Huh?

90
00:05:03,300 --> 00:05:04,470
Don't think for a second

91
00:05:04,510 --> 00:05:06,510
you're getting away
with what you've done.

92
00:05:06,560 --> 00:05:10,060
One way or another,
I'm making you pay.

93
00:05:10,100 --> 00:05:11,480
[Yamaha grunts]

94
00:05:14,900 --> 00:05:16,020
[Danji gasps]

95
00:05:17,230 --> 00:05:18,940
[Danji gasps, grunts]

96
00:05:24,450 --> 00:05:26,410
[RIGHT] Do as we please?

97
00:05:26,450 --> 00:05:28,830
Understood! [grunts]

98
00:05:33,250 --> 00:05:35,540
[RIGHT] I'll get the villagers
somewhere safe.

99
00:05:35,580 --> 00:05:37,340
Watch out, kid.

100
00:05:37,380 --> 00:05:39,010
My other half is hot-blooded.

101
00:05:39,050 --> 00:05:40,340
[Gabby gasps]

102
00:05:43,550 --> 00:05:44,850
[Gabby gasps]

103
00:05:47,260 --> 00:05:49,390
[LEFT] You heard my master.

104
00:05:49,430 --> 00:05:51,600
I am to do as I please.

105
00:05:54,190 --> 00:05:55,730
[Gabby yells]

106
00:05:57,820 --> 00:05:59,360
He's loading another!

107
00:06:00,070 --> 00:06:01,940
[Gabriel growls]

108
00:06:05,870 --> 00:06:06,910
[Yuru gasps]

109
00:06:06,950 --> 00:06:09,120
They show resilience, that lot.

110
00:06:09,160 --> 00:06:11,790
-[YURU] I'll chase!
-Whoa! Ah, jeez.

111
00:06:11,830 --> 00:06:13,210
Why bother?

112
00:06:13,250 --> 00:06:14,920
Let's get off this mountain
already!

113
00:06:14,960 --> 00:06:17,000
♪

114
00:06:25,340 --> 00:06:27,550
[RIGHT] Oy... You alive?

115
00:06:27,600 --> 00:06:29,560
-[Azami groans]
-[RIGHT] Oy!

116
00:06:31,680 --> 00:06:33,480
[RIGHT] Oh! You are.

117
00:06:33,520 --> 00:06:34,850
[AZAMI] Huh?

118
00:06:37,520 --> 00:06:39,770
[RIGHT] Must be
someone else's blood.

119
00:06:39,820 --> 00:06:42,530
You're unharmed.
That's good!

120
00:06:42,570 --> 00:06:44,150
[footsteps]

121
00:06:44,490 --> 00:06:45,530
[AZAMI] Huh?

122
00:06:45,780 --> 00:06:48,660
[RIGHT] Oh, I always forget,
you silly mortals.

123
00:06:48,700 --> 00:06:50,040
You can't see me.

124
00:06:50,080 --> 00:06:51,330
[Azami gasps]

125
00:06:51,370 --> 00:06:53,660
Not to worry, young'un!

126
00:06:53,700 --> 00:06:55,120
I am no monster.

127
00:06:55,170 --> 00:06:56,960
I'm here to take you
somewhere safe,

128
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:58,710
-without any bad guys!
-[thuds]

129
00:06:58,750 --> 00:06:59,880
[RIGHT] Uh?

130
00:07:00,590 --> 00:07:01,750
Uh-oh.

131
00:07:05,050 --> 00:07:06,340
Insulting.

132
00:07:06,380 --> 00:07:09,550
Everyone of these kids
fainted when they saw me.

133
00:07:09,600 --> 00:07:11,220
That kinda hurts!

134
00:07:12,180 --> 00:07:14,100
They butchered
every adult they found...

135
00:07:14,140 --> 00:07:15,940
-[footsteps running]
-...but didn't lay a finger

136
00:07:15,980 --> 00:07:17,400
on the children.

137
00:07:17,640 --> 00:07:19,190
[ASA] Uh?

138
00:07:20,810 --> 00:07:23,940
Oh, you see me, don't you?

139
00:07:25,030 --> 00:07:26,110
[Asa grunts]

140
00:07:26,150 --> 00:07:27,410
[RIGHT] Huh?

141
00:07:30,950 --> 00:07:33,660
[Right yelling]

142
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,330
[Asa grunts]

143
00:07:38,040 --> 00:07:41,250
Cheeky brat,
not even a fond greeting?

144
00:07:41,300 --> 00:07:43,670
And that's one
dangerous power you got.

145
00:07:43,710 --> 00:07:46,170
Normally, I'd be more than happy
to give you a fight,

146
00:07:46,220 --> 00:07:49,090
but my master ordered...
[coughs] Uh?

147
00:07:49,140 --> 00:07:50,760
[grunts] Come on!

148
00:07:50,800 --> 00:07:52,600
Kids just don't have
the kind of respect

149
00:07:52,640 --> 00:07:54,600
they had in my day! [scoffs]

150
00:07:56,100 --> 00:07:57,940
[sniffs]

151
00:07:59,650 --> 00:08:01,810
[RIGHT] That lass...

152
00:08:02,190 --> 00:08:03,860
[Gabby grunts]

153
00:08:05,820 --> 00:08:07,400
[Gabriel grunting]

154
00:08:15,120 --> 00:08:18,330
[GABBY] You're kidding me.
I'm losing a two v one?

155
00:08:18,370 --> 00:08:20,420
[Gabriel grunting]

156
00:08:22,380 --> 00:08:23,920
[Left grunting]

157
00:08:30,720 --> 00:08:31,930
[Gabby gasps]

158
00:08:35,220 --> 00:08:36,600
[Left grunts]

159
00:08:38,180 --> 00:08:39,480
[Gabby grunts]

160
00:08:39,520 --> 00:08:42,020
Not again!

161
00:08:42,940 --> 00:08:43,980
Asa!

162
00:08:53,030 --> 00:08:53,990
Damn!

163
00:08:54,030 --> 00:08:55,240
[Gabby grunts]

164
00:08:55,280 --> 00:08:56,620
[ASA] I got you!

165
00:08:57,450 --> 00:08:59,660
Thanks, you saved my bacon.

166
00:08:59,710 --> 00:09:00,910
[YURU] Don't move!

167
00:09:03,630 --> 00:09:06,300
You're going to tell me
who you are. Right now!

168
00:09:06,340 --> 00:09:09,090
I am your little sister.
Like I had said.

169
00:09:09,130 --> 00:09:11,970
[YURU] Don't lie to me!
You're way taller than Asa!

170
00:09:12,010 --> 00:09:13,680
[ASA] The food's
much more nutritious

171
00:09:13,720 --> 00:09:15,390
when you go down the mountain.

172
00:09:15,430 --> 00:09:17,930
[YURU] You're also
too mean-looking to be Asa!

173
00:09:17,970 --> 00:09:20,430
[ASA] Life's been tough.
I'm a bit jaded.

174
00:09:22,230 --> 00:09:23,520
[Right shouts] Oy!

175
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:26,570
Family shouldn't draw arms
against each other!

176
00:09:31,400 --> 00:09:33,030
She ain't lying.

177
00:09:33,070 --> 00:09:36,080
I could smell the lass' blood,
and it was the same as yours.

178
00:09:36,120 --> 00:09:37,540
You're siblings.

179
00:09:37,580 --> 00:09:38,620
[YURU] Huh?

180
00:09:38,660 --> 00:09:40,410
Then, if you're the real Asa,

181
00:09:40,460 --> 00:09:42,790
who's the person who's been up
in the keep all these years?

182
00:09:42,830 --> 00:09:44,290
-[ASA] An impostor.
-[Yuru gasps]

183
00:09:45,170 --> 00:09:46,250
♪

184
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:49,840
[ASA] Ten years ago,
our parents grabbed me

185
00:09:49,880 --> 00:09:53,220
and said we needed to run away
from the village in a hurry.

186
00:09:53,260 --> 00:09:54,550
Afterward,

187
00:09:54,680 --> 00:09:57,600
Granny and the others
feared you'd leave, as well.

188
00:09:59,890 --> 00:10:01,230
To avoid that,

189
00:10:01,270 --> 00:10:03,440
they created a new Asa,

190
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:05,900
designed to keep you
chained here.

191
00:10:05,940 --> 00:10:08,690
You'd never leave
your little sister all alone,

192
00:10:08,730 --> 00:10:12,820
so they exploited your kindness
as a diligent older brother.

193
00:10:12,860 --> 00:10:15,610
The real Asa
is the one you see here,

194
00:10:15,660 --> 00:10:16,820
the one in front of you.

195
00:10:16,870 --> 00:10:19,370
[Yuru gasps]

196
00:10:23,040 --> 00:10:26,330
[Yuru grunts softly,
breathes shakily]

197
00:10:28,210 --> 00:10:29,380
You came here to have

198
00:10:29,420 --> 00:10:31,340
that touching reunion,
didn't you?

199
00:10:31,380 --> 00:10:34,720
Well, you got it,
so please back off, all right?

200
00:10:34,760 --> 00:10:36,220
Dera, are you...

201
00:10:36,260 --> 00:10:38,510
They're trying to get
their hands on you.

202
00:10:38,550 --> 00:10:40,680
We know this
alleged Asa is strong,

203
00:10:40,720 --> 00:10:42,560
but we don't know how strong.

204
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:44,390
If we drag this out here,

205
00:10:44,440 --> 00:10:46,480
the village will pay the price.

206
00:10:46,520 --> 00:10:47,610
[Yuru gasps]

207
00:10:47,900 --> 00:10:50,400
[DERA] There are still survivors
to worry about.

208
00:10:50,440 --> 00:10:52,240
[Yuru grunts softly]

209
00:10:53,740 --> 00:10:55,530
[breathes shakily]

210
00:10:59,080 --> 00:11:00,530
-[YURU] Listen...
-[BOTH] Hm?

211
00:11:01,120 --> 00:11:03,700
You're gonna leave
the rest of the village alone.

212
00:11:03,750 --> 00:11:06,540
In exchange,
I'll let the runt walk away.

213
00:11:06,580 --> 00:11:07,790
All right?

214
00:11:08,460 --> 00:11:10,920
-[ASA] It's a deal.
-Asa!

215
00:11:10,960 --> 00:11:12,670
See you.

216
00:11:17,970 --> 00:11:19,510
[whooshing]

217
00:11:22,720 --> 00:11:23,930
[Gabby grunts]

218
00:11:23,980 --> 00:11:26,270
Why aren't we capturing him?

219
00:11:26,310 --> 00:11:28,650
[ASA] Because your wounds
need urgent attention.

220
00:11:28,690 --> 00:11:31,520
At least we know he's safe,
so this mission was a success.

221
00:11:31,570 --> 00:11:32,900
[Gabby grunts]

222
00:11:32,940 --> 00:11:34,240
[ASA] Are you okay?

223
00:11:35,530 --> 00:11:37,990
You know, your brother
is a decent shot.

224
00:11:39,030 --> 00:11:41,410
-He really got me.
-Yeah.

225
00:11:41,780 --> 00:11:44,870
-He's merciless, too.
-Yeah.

226
00:11:44,910 --> 00:11:47,160
[GABBY] Least he's alive.

227
00:11:47,210 --> 00:11:48,710
[ASA] Yeah.

228
00:11:48,750 --> 00:11:50,080
He's alive.

229
00:11:50,920 --> 00:11:53,170
[Asa cries softly]

230
00:11:55,170 --> 00:11:58,510
My big brother.
He's still alive.

231
00:11:59,220 --> 00:12:00,470
♪

232
00:12:01,600 --> 00:12:03,560
[Asa continues crying]

233
00:12:07,060 --> 00:12:09,400
-[soft rumbling]
-[GABRIEL] Huh?

234
00:12:09,440 --> 00:12:11,020
[Asa continues crying]

235
00:12:18,490 --> 00:12:20,320
[GABBY] Barrier's back up.

236
00:12:20,990 --> 00:12:22,740
We need to get out of here.

237
00:12:39,430 --> 00:12:40,970
DAEMONS OF THE SHADOW REALM

238
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:43,100
[MAN] Those helicopters
sure were loud.

239
00:12:43,140 --> 00:12:44,100
OLD HIGASHI VILLAGE TRAILHEAD

240
00:12:44,140 --> 00:12:45,390
Wonder what was happening.

241
00:12:45,430 --> 00:12:48,020
Maybe someone
was in danger up there.

242
00:12:48,060 --> 00:12:49,100
From what I hear,

243
00:12:49,140 --> 00:12:50,600
people go missing
on this mountain

244
00:12:50,640 --> 00:12:51,770
from time to time.

245
00:12:51,810 --> 00:12:52,810
There are even a handful

246
00:12:52,860 --> 00:12:54,520
who've never been
heard from again.

247
00:12:54,570 --> 00:12:56,650
[sighs]
It's like a horror story.

248
00:12:56,690 --> 00:12:58,240
You know, the one that I mean.

249
00:12:58,280 --> 00:12:59,360
What was it?

250
00:12:59,450 --> 00:13:01,530
-Oh, the lost village!
-Yeah, that's it!

251
00:13:01,570 --> 00:13:04,830
Hikers find themselves wandering
into an alternate world

252
00:13:04,870 --> 00:13:06,200
without even realizing.

253
00:13:06,240 --> 00:13:07,330
There's a village there,

254
00:13:07,370 --> 00:13:09,120
even though maps say
there shouldn't be.

255
00:13:09,160 --> 00:13:10,870
But when they try
to go back later,

256
00:13:10,910 --> 00:13:13,290
the whole place has disappeared
without a trace.

257
00:13:13,330 --> 00:13:15,340
[DERA] Hello, folks!

258
00:13:15,380 --> 00:13:16,500
Hi.

259
00:13:16,880 --> 00:13:18,340
Hey there, gentlemen.

260
00:13:18,380 --> 00:13:21,090
-Were those mountain porters?
-Dressed up like that?

261
00:13:21,130 --> 00:13:22,430
-[wind blows]
-[both scream]

262
00:13:22,470 --> 00:13:23,930
[WOMAN] The wind's crazy!

263
00:13:23,970 --> 00:13:25,850
[MAN] I think we're done here!

264
00:13:28,350 --> 00:13:31,270
Good. We can't see
the village anymore.

265
00:13:31,310 --> 00:13:33,310
The barrier must be up again.

266
00:13:33,350 --> 00:13:35,570
[YURU] Does that mean
we can never go back?

267
00:13:35,610 --> 00:13:37,150
[DERA]
Well, if you really want to,

268
00:13:37,190 --> 00:13:39,070
it's not impossible.

269
00:13:39,110 --> 00:13:41,650
But now, there are people
who know where the village is,

270
00:13:41,700 --> 00:13:43,110
and how to get inside of it.

271
00:13:43,160 --> 00:13:44,700
Considering that
you're their target,

272
00:13:44,740 --> 00:13:47,660
I don't think a hiding place
like that will do you much good.

273
00:13:47,700 --> 00:13:51,040
Best keep away, and blend in
with the world below.

274
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:54,210
Hang a right.

275
00:14:00,260 --> 00:14:02,760
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

276
00:14:03,380 --> 00:14:06,300
Appreciate you waitin' for us!
Thanks, Hana!

277
00:14:06,350 --> 00:14:08,680
Hey, what's goin' on, Dera?

278
00:14:08,720 --> 00:14:11,020
All you said was you were
bringing a human back with you,

279
00:14:11,060 --> 00:14:12,730
so why are there daemons too?

280
00:14:14,060 --> 00:14:15,940
-[RIGHT] Oh!
-So, she's a seer.

281
00:14:15,980 --> 00:14:17,570
Sorry!

282
00:14:17,900 --> 00:14:20,440
[DERA] I know this is a lot,
but we've gotta run.

283
00:14:20,490 --> 00:14:23,490
I'll get you caught up
as we make our escape.

284
00:14:23,530 --> 00:14:25,410
Yuru's life is at risk here.

285
00:14:25,450 --> 00:14:27,780
So, this kid's
one of the twins, huh?

286
00:14:27,830 --> 00:14:30,200
And our friends here
are the Left and the Right.

287
00:14:30,240 --> 00:14:32,710
Oy! What's this contraption?

288
00:14:32,750 --> 00:14:34,790
It is a giant metal beast.

289
00:14:34,830 --> 00:14:37,130
Well, they seem occupied.

290
00:14:37,170 --> 00:14:38,790
Nice to meet you, Yuru.

291
00:14:38,840 --> 00:14:40,000
Ah, likewise.

292
00:14:40,460 --> 00:14:41,800
Just call me Hana.

293
00:14:41,840 --> 00:14:45,090
Dera's junior. We work together
as daemon retainers.

294
00:14:45,130 --> 00:14:47,760
Mind if I ask if those noses
are pickin' up

295
00:14:47,800 --> 00:14:49,890
any other daemons nearby?

296
00:14:49,930 --> 00:14:51,560
Seems like we're in the clear.

297
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:53,770
Then what do you say
we get somewhere crowded

298
00:14:53,810 --> 00:14:55,480
before that stops
being the case?

299
00:14:55,520 --> 00:14:57,650
-Get in, Yuru!
-Get in this thing?

300
00:14:57,690 --> 00:15:01,190
I don't even know what it is,
much less what it does!

301
00:15:01,440 --> 00:15:02,690
Fair enough.

302
00:15:02,740 --> 00:15:05,280
This "thing" is called
an automobile.

303
00:15:05,320 --> 00:15:07,620
So, it's used for traveling.

304
00:15:07,660 --> 00:15:10,240
Uh, right! It's made
of metal and junk.

305
00:15:10,280 --> 00:15:12,870
And this nice lady here
is the driver.

306
00:15:12,910 --> 00:15:14,410
Uh, what else?

307
00:15:14,460 --> 00:15:15,710
[engine starts]

308
00:15:16,250 --> 00:15:17,540
Forget the rest of it,

309
00:15:17,580 --> 00:15:19,670
there are horses in here,
and it goes real fast!

310
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:22,250
Makes sense.

311
00:15:22,300 --> 00:15:23,800
[LEFT] Understood.

312
00:15:23,840 --> 00:15:24,970
[YURU] Right.

313
00:15:25,840 --> 00:15:27,220
[DERA] Seriously?

314
00:15:28,130 --> 00:15:29,260
OLD HIGASHI VILLAGE TRAILHEAD

315
00:15:29,510 --> 00:15:31,300
[GABBY] Stupid ride's
taking forever to get here.

316
00:15:31,350 --> 00:15:33,390
You're sure we're not
still inside the barrier,

317
00:15:33,430 --> 00:15:35,390
and they're lookin'
everywhere for us?

318
00:15:35,430 --> 00:15:37,850
If that were true,
I wouldn't have any data.

319
00:15:37,900 --> 00:15:39,230
WE'RE AT THE SIGN 2 KM FROM THE
OLD HIGASHI VILLAGE TRAILHEAD

320
00:15:39,270 --> 00:15:41,020
[ASA] Not like it'd matter
if we were inside of it.

321
00:15:41,070 --> 00:15:42,400
I'd just bust it open again.

322
00:15:42,440 --> 00:15:43,650
[footsteps]

323
00:15:43,690 --> 00:15:45,030
[JIN] Found them.

324
00:15:45,820 --> 00:15:47,320
Thank you for waiting.

325
00:15:47,360 --> 00:15:49,160
Sorry you had such a rough time.

326
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:51,780
Thanks, Jinny, nice to see you!

327
00:15:51,830 --> 00:15:52,910
I appreciate you

328
00:15:53,120 --> 00:15:55,000
coming all the way up
the mountain for us, Jin.

329
00:15:55,040 --> 00:15:57,710
I heard some unexpected
daemons crashed your party.

330
00:15:57,750 --> 00:16:00,540
Makes me wonder if I could've
turned the tides being there.

331
00:16:00,590 --> 00:16:03,170
Prepare the stretcher
for Miss Gabby.

332
00:16:03,210 --> 00:16:05,510
So, kiddo, how bad
are your wounds?

333
00:16:05,550 --> 00:16:07,050
[GABBY]
They've stopped bleeding.

334
00:16:07,090 --> 00:16:09,090
Still have an arrowhead
in my shoulder

335
00:16:09,130 --> 00:16:10,850
I'll need removed later, though.

336
00:16:10,890 --> 00:16:13,050
But we got the one
in my leg out clean.

337
00:16:13,100 --> 00:16:14,640
[JIN] Those are both serious.

338
00:16:14,680 --> 00:16:17,100
Don't talk about them
like some casual thing.

339
00:16:17,140 --> 00:16:19,310
I'm fine, no biggie, man.

340
00:16:19,350 --> 00:16:21,440
I'm used to dealing with pain.

341
00:16:22,400 --> 00:16:23,900
Well, I'm concerned to see

342
00:16:23,940 --> 00:16:25,490
that your brother
isn't with you.

343
00:16:25,530 --> 00:16:27,150
He got away.

344
00:16:27,610 --> 00:16:29,950
[JIN] So you did confirm
his existence?

345
00:16:29,990 --> 00:16:31,570
He's alive and in good health.

346
00:16:32,240 --> 00:16:34,240
[GABBY] Couldn't catch a glimpse
on your way up to us?

347
00:16:34,280 --> 00:16:36,330
Didn't see any sign of him
as we came up,

348
00:16:36,370 --> 00:16:38,460
even though we made sure
to secure all the trailheads.

349
00:16:38,500 --> 00:16:40,920
They must have a shortcut
that we don't know about.

350
00:16:40,960 --> 00:16:42,960
There's a possibility
they're still on the mountain.

351
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:45,840
-[MAN 3] If we had choppers.
-[Jin groans]

352
00:16:46,170 --> 00:16:48,720
We lost two helicopters
and all of our soldiers.

353
00:16:48,760 --> 00:16:51,220
The old man's gonna
have my head.

354
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:52,800
Gotcha covered, Jinny!

355
00:16:52,850 --> 00:16:53,930
We can at least tell you

356
00:16:54,140 --> 00:16:56,100
Asa's brother escaped
with some guy named Dera.

357
00:16:56,640 --> 00:16:57,810
[JIN] Dera?

358
00:16:58,180 --> 00:17:00,560
[GABBY] Probably the same guy
who killed all our soldiers.

359
00:17:00,600 --> 00:17:02,940
Mr. Kagemori, could that be...

360
00:17:02,980 --> 00:17:04,150
[grunts]

361
00:17:04,320 --> 00:17:06,020
[JIN] It's the Tadera.

362
00:17:06,070 --> 00:17:07,900
Of all days,
how'd we pick one

363
00:17:07,940 --> 00:17:10,650
when a Tadera retainer
was here?

364
00:17:11,400 --> 00:17:12,910
That proves it.

365
00:17:12,950 --> 00:17:15,910
I should've brought
my pair along, after all.

366
00:17:16,870 --> 00:17:19,830
[DERA] So to sum it up,
we released the Left and Right,

367
00:17:19,870 --> 00:17:21,500
they took down some choppers,

368
00:17:21,540 --> 00:17:23,840
then kicked some
enemy daemon butt.

369
00:17:23,880 --> 00:17:25,800
I offed most
of the soldiers I found,

370
00:17:25,840 --> 00:17:28,800
but there were so many,
I'm pretty sure a lot got away.

371
00:17:28,840 --> 00:17:30,720
It takes a special kind
of pain in the ass

372
00:17:30,760 --> 00:17:33,340
to send a bunch of soldiers
after one single kid.

373
00:17:33,390 --> 00:17:34,760
You're tellin' me.

374
00:17:34,800 --> 00:17:36,720
Figure it must've been
the Kagemori.

375
00:17:36,760 --> 00:17:37,930
Are you for real?

376
00:17:38,060 --> 00:17:40,930
[DERA] I guess they got my face
and name now.

377
00:17:40,980 --> 00:17:42,520
I'll have to shave.

378
00:17:42,560 --> 00:17:44,440
Probably move, too.

379
00:17:44,900 --> 00:17:48,280
[HANA] Ah! All I wanted
was a peaceful life.

380
00:17:52,490 --> 00:17:54,700
[LEFT] I sense daemons
approaching rapidly.

381
00:17:54,740 --> 00:17:55,910
Seriously?

382
00:17:55,950 --> 00:17:58,620
[DERA]
Great, we're being tailed?

383
00:17:58,660 --> 00:18:00,910
[HANA] Come on, we just left!

384
00:18:00,950 --> 00:18:02,250
[Left scoffs]

385
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:07,340
[LEFT] Fret not,
these two mean us no harm.

386
00:18:07,380 --> 00:18:09,050
We know them well.

387
00:18:09,130 --> 00:18:11,170
♪

388
00:18:16,930 --> 00:18:19,310
[OSHIRASAMA] I'm pleased
to see you, my friends.

389
00:18:19,350 --> 00:18:21,390
Since you've manifested here,

390
00:18:21,430 --> 00:18:23,560
does that mean you've
found yourselves a new master?

391
00:18:23,600 --> 00:18:26,100
Aye.
After being up there so long,

392
00:18:26,150 --> 00:18:28,070
everything here seems foreign!

393
00:18:28,110 --> 00:18:30,190
It has been nearly 400 years.

394
00:18:30,230 --> 00:18:32,900
[RIGHT] Our new master
is the boy inside there.

395
00:18:32,950 --> 00:18:34,490
[OSHIRASAMA]
Oh, that's wonderful!

396
00:18:34,530 --> 00:18:36,200
I love children.

397
00:18:36,240 --> 00:18:38,830
It just so happens,
he's one of the twins

398
00:18:38,870 --> 00:18:40,160
who sunders night and day.

399
00:18:42,620 --> 00:18:44,410
You've quite the challenge.

400
00:18:44,460 --> 00:18:45,580
[horse neighs]

401
00:18:45,630 --> 00:18:47,880
What do you plan to do now?

402
00:18:47,920 --> 00:18:49,050
No clue.

403
00:18:49,210 --> 00:18:51,710
They say we can hide inside
some busy human town

404
00:18:51,760 --> 00:18:53,090
for the time being.

405
00:18:53,130 --> 00:18:54,380
[OSHIRASAMA] Ah...

406
00:18:54,420 --> 00:18:58,050
You must tell me all about it
when you return.

407
00:18:59,720 --> 00:19:01,310
Fare thee well!

408
00:19:01,350 --> 00:19:03,560
[horse neighs]

409
00:19:04,310 --> 00:19:06,980
They were here?
They were here!

410
00:19:07,020 --> 00:19:08,110
They were here!

411
00:19:08,150 --> 00:19:09,690
They really do exist!

412
00:19:09,730 --> 00:19:11,610
A horse? So what?

413
00:19:11,650 --> 00:19:13,230
Show some respect!

414
00:19:13,280 --> 00:19:15,280
[HANA] That was Oshirasama!

415
00:19:15,320 --> 00:19:16,820
[DERA] They're a legit god!

416
00:19:16,860 --> 00:19:19,280
They're nothing like
your average daemon!

417
00:19:19,330 --> 00:19:21,080
-Legit?
-[DERA] It means real!

418
00:19:21,120 --> 00:19:23,120
I never thought I'd get
the chance to see them

419
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:24,200
while I'm still alive!

420
00:19:24,250 --> 00:19:27,580
Ah! Life really
can be beautiful!

421
00:19:27,630 --> 00:19:29,040
Do they not understand

422
00:19:29,090 --> 00:19:31,960
we are the gods of the village
they just came from?

423
00:19:32,010 --> 00:19:34,970
I detect a slight disparity
in treatment.

424
00:19:35,010 --> 00:19:37,630
[YURU] So there's
a variety of demons?

425
00:19:37,680 --> 00:19:38,760
[HANA] Sure are.

426
00:19:38,800 --> 00:19:40,430
Us humans have a tendency

427
00:19:40,470 --> 00:19:42,310
to sort them
into different genres.

428
00:19:42,350 --> 00:19:43,430
[YURU] Genres?

429
00:19:43,720 --> 00:19:47,060
[HANA] I should've said types,
or maybe categories?

430
00:19:47,100 --> 00:19:49,980
We call some of them gods,
or spirits.

431
00:19:50,020 --> 00:19:51,820
Some are like Oshirasama

432
00:19:51,860 --> 00:19:54,780
and live a relaxed life
alongside humans.

433
00:19:54,820 --> 00:19:56,650
Others bring good fortune,

434
00:19:56,700 --> 00:19:57,990
but some are tricksters

435
00:19:58,030 --> 00:20:00,280
that drive humans
to criminal activity.

436
00:20:00,320 --> 00:20:02,080
[DERA] Those dentures
that attacked us

437
00:20:02,120 --> 00:20:04,040
seemed all-in as a combat type.

438
00:20:04,080 --> 00:20:06,500
It's a pair of upper
and lower jaws.

439
00:20:06,870 --> 00:20:09,540
I've heard of daemons like that
eating their masters,

440
00:20:09,580 --> 00:20:10,880
if they mistreat 'em.

441
00:20:11,590 --> 00:20:13,630
I'm really sorry,
it's my fault.

442
00:20:13,670 --> 00:20:15,590
I made the final call
to let him go.

443
00:20:15,630 --> 00:20:18,180
If anyone has to be reprimanded,
then let it be me.

444
00:20:18,220 --> 00:20:20,390
You can't go takin'
all the blame.

445
00:20:20,430 --> 00:20:22,600
You only did it to protect me.

446
00:20:22,640 --> 00:20:24,970
No need to sweat
the details, you two.

447
00:20:25,020 --> 00:20:26,850
The old man
will be happy to know

448
00:20:26,890 --> 00:20:28,480
he's alive and off the mountain.

449
00:20:28,520 --> 00:20:30,520
So to that end,
the mission succeeded.

450
00:20:30,560 --> 00:20:33,070
Still wanna make it clear
how toast I would've been

451
00:20:33,110 --> 00:20:34,900
if Asa hadn't been there
to bail me out.

452
00:20:34,940 --> 00:20:37,860
Are you saying his daemons
were that dangerous?

453
00:20:37,900 --> 00:20:40,200
[GABBY] Well, they were
nothing to scoff at,

454
00:20:40,240 --> 00:20:43,160
but it was the kid
who shot me with his bow.

455
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:45,330
First he shut down my mobility,

456
00:20:45,370 --> 00:20:46,870
then my dominant hand.

457
00:20:46,910 --> 00:20:49,040
[JIN] Oof. Scary brother
you got there.

458
00:20:49,080 --> 00:20:50,750
[ASA] You should've seen him,

459
00:20:50,790 --> 00:20:53,250
he's got the mind
of a die-hard hunter!

460
00:20:53,290 --> 00:20:54,750
[thunder rumbling]

461
00:20:54,800 --> 00:20:56,800
[rain pouring]

462
00:20:58,460 --> 00:21:01,430
[men grunting]

463
00:21:02,100 --> 00:21:03,220
[MAN 1] Damn it.

464
00:21:03,260 --> 00:21:05,640
The rain's starting
to really come down.

465
00:21:05,680 --> 00:21:07,890
If we don't meet up
with Mr. Kagemori soon,

466
00:21:07,930 --> 00:21:09,940
they're probably gonna
leave us behind.

467
00:21:09,980 --> 00:21:11,770
-Let's go...
-[both gasp]

468
00:21:11,810 --> 00:21:13,730
[MAN 1] You're kidding me.

469
00:21:15,980 --> 00:21:17,530
[grunts]

470
00:21:17,860 --> 00:21:20,610
We've been to this spot
five times already.

471
00:21:21,360 --> 00:21:22,950
We're screwed.

472
00:21:22,990 --> 00:21:24,530
We can't leave.

473
00:21:24,580 --> 00:21:25,910
[thunder rumbling]

474
00:21:25,950 --> 00:21:27,790
[vehicles passing by]

475
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:29,750
♪

476
00:21:55,230 --> 00:21:57,480
[♪ closing theme song playing]

477
00:23:26,530 --> 00:23:27,910
NEXT EPISODE
PREVIEW

478
00:23:28,030 --> 00:23:30,870
[YURU] Flush when you're done.
Make sure it goes down.

479
00:23:30,910 --> 00:23:32,120
We're in Guntama.

480
00:23:32,160 --> 00:23:33,330
[LEFT] Yes, Guntama.

481
00:23:33,370 --> 00:23:35,040
[HANA] You got
another thing comin'

482
00:23:35,080 --> 00:23:36,870
if you think I'd ever marry you!

483
00:23:36,920 --> 00:23:39,960
EPISODE 3
"DERA AND HANA"
